cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Logroño replication of Vogelbacher et al. (2026): building-level pluvial flood risk with open data, tested against recorded flood impacts"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
abstract: "FORRT replication of Vogelbacher et al. (2026, NHESS) in Logroño, Spain, with open data only (REACHOUT flood maps, Spanish Cadastre, INE Census 2021, Copernicus Urban Atlas). Building-level pluvial flood risk is computed for the whole city with building-climate-risk, and the framework's flood hazard is compared with places where storms caused flooding in 2018-2024, at street scale and at census-section scale. Snakemake pipeline from download to figures."
type: software
authors:
- family-names: "Fouilloux"
  given-names: "Anne"
  orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1784-2920"
  affiliation: "LifeWatch ERIC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/annefou/logrono-pluvial-flood-replication"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-10-10"
# Identifiers below are recorded AUTOMATICALLY on each release by
# .github/workflows/release-identifiers.yml — don't fill them in by hand.
#
# `doi:` is the CONCEPT DOI: it means "cite this project" and deliberately
# resolves to whatever version is latest. That floating behaviour is correct
# HERE and wrong in a nanopub — see scripts/set_release_identifiers.py.
#
# (This used to say "run /init-template again or edit by hand". /init-template
# deletes itself as its final step, so by the time a DOI existed the skill it
# named was gone and "edit by hand" was the only path left. Two repos built from
# this template then recorded the version DOI two different ways — one a
# structured identifier, one a prose comment. Hence the automation.)
